# The build context for Dockerfile.keeper, which BuildKit reads instead of
# .dockerignore because it is named after that Dockerfile.
#
# The keeper is built from two modules — tools/, and the extension's own sources
# that tools/go.mod replaces in from ../ — so the context is wider than the
# extension image's. It stays a listed set even so: the extension image's context
# is filtered for reproducibility, this one to keep .env files, keys and build
# output from ever being reachable in a layer.

# ignore everything
*

# the extension module, as far as the tooling's replace directive reaches into it:
# pkg/ and the two manifests. internal/ and cmd/ are not imported from tools/.
!go.mod
!go.sum
!pkg/

# the tooling module, which is what is built here
!tools/

# the deployed addresses, the one repository file the keeper reads at runtime;
# the CHAIN build arg picks which chain's is baked in
!deploy/config/*/deployed-addresses.json

# nothing generated, and nothing holding a secret, from any of the above
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
.env*
*.env
out/
